<Project>

  <!--
    Intentionally empty — this file exists to STOP MSBuild's upward search, not to configure
    anything.

    MSBuild walks up the directory tree from each project until it finds a
    Directory.Build.targets and imports the first one it hits. This repo has a
    Directory.Build.props, which terminates the equivalent walk for props — but with no
    Directory.Build.targets, the targets search escaped the repository entirely and kept
    climbing.

    That matters because wham is consumed as a git submodule: WarHub/battlescribe-spec
    vendors it at .deps/wham, so when that repo added a root Directory.Build.targets it was
    silently imported into every wham project. wham's build became a property of wherever it
    happened to be checked out rather than of wham itself — and the failure mode is quiet,
    since an inherited targets file usually builds fine right up until it doesn't.

    Repo-wide targets, if this repo ever needs any, belong here.
  -->

</Project>
